{"title":"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A sector with acute central angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is cut from a circle of radius 6. The radius of the circle circumscribed about the sector is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/1/8b1c6765381f707887fd23c142d3fcc11166399e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 3\\cos\\theta \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 3\\sec\\theta \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 3 \\cos \\frac12 \\theta \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 3 \\sec \\frac12 \\theta \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"530\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the center of the circle and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f642cbbd390b4882363ab6b5c2906dbf6be6cc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> be two points on the circle such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/b/40bb7d97e256f7863394c099bf086e692619bfb0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AOB = \\theta$\" width=\"88\" height=\"13\" />.  If the circle circumscribes the sector, then the circle must circumscribe <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/4/e44c01c0ed926b86414a0fbedc2fe1d2eaa9b871.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle AOB$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/8/ba8a014f7172e42a9e0dbcb09ed13df730ff0299.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((-120,-160)--(0,0)--(120,-160)); draw((-60,-80)--(0,-125)--(60,-80),dotted); draw((0,0)--(0,-125)); draw(arc((0,0),200,233.13,306.87)); dot((0,0)); label(&quot;O&quot;,(0,0),N); dot((-120,-160)); label(&quot;A&quot;,(-120,-160),SW); dot((120,-160)); label(&quot;B&quot;,(120,-160),SE); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"198\" />\n</p><p>Draw the perpendicular bisectors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/a/b7a762ac8b4e23ffdd778ad6d5a8b97df8c7ce01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0964c9cf406ef8e5ec8beaa6a92125f2d8f90460.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and mark the intersection as point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and draw a line from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  By HL Congruency and CPCTC, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/4/ff4b63ee34bf2790717b394ad1803da0fe54fc0d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AOC = \\angle BOC = \\theta /2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"186\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the circumradius of the triangle.  Using the definition of cosine for right triangles,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/5/5b56dbf79de14c19cc60258aed5a1bed0c1f695a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos (\\theta /2) = \\frac{3}{R}\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/9/149ec257c363b9d872e6755673d4ac3f25be910c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[R = \\frac{3}{\\cos (\\theta /2)}\\]\" width=\"105\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef00abe047eb4e03aa85b712b91f7605e9f5bb31.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[R = 3 \\sec (\\theta /2)\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" />\nAnswer choices A, C, and E are smaller, so they are eliminated.  However, as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> aproaches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22ec0d2e4202839322d26a23dcb13f79821df5d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />, the value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30c628fa701820d482e3eb2878f33687ed17b1e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\sec\\theta$\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> would approach infinity while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/9/c99dacfdf9be10c6f96fd1b29ec0bc7dfc7e696b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\sec \\tfrac12 \\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"57\" height=\"21\" /> would approach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/5/c1550ed903519235abb8b073236d627dc43b1ade.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.  A super large circle would definitely not be a circumcircle if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is close to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22ec0d2e4202839322d26a23dcb13f79821df5d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />, so we can confirm that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/0/c601170bc7febe347c89f9e7a581060ce083c417.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 3 \\sec \\frac12 \\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"107\" height=\"48\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME\" title=\"1973 AHSME\">1973 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1973 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1973\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1973_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1973 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selfli